	(text "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N8R2 (U9, LCSC C2913204) - replaces ESP32-WROOM-32 for native USB on the single USB-C port\nUSB: GPIO19 = USB_DN, GPIO20 = USB_DP -> USBLC6 (usbc_pd sheet) -> USB-C J17. Default: built-in USB-Serial-JTAG\n(CDC console + flashing, no DTR/RTS needed). Application firmware may switch to TinyUSB OTG: CDC + MSC (SD card).\nRecovery: hold BOOT (B3, GPIO0) and press RESET (B4, EN) -> ROM download mode over USB-Serial-JTAG.\nSD card: owned by ESP32-S3 (SDMMC 4-bit, same GPIOs as before: CLK 14, CMD 15, D0 2, D1 4, D2 12, D3 13), card detect\nSD_CD on GPIO10 (pull-up R86, low = card inserted). FPGA bank-6 SD pins stay connected: FPGA must keep them Hi-Z.\nECP5 programming: ESP32-S3 bit-bangs JTAG (TCK 18, TMS 5, TDI 16, TDO 17) to SRAM or the config flash.\nADC SPI: SDO GPIO6, DIN GPIO21, SCK GPIO8, CNV GPIO9. FPGA links: GPIO0/1/40/41, UART0 TXD/RXD.\nR56 pulls GPIO0 high (normal boot); EN has RC delay R34/R35 + C81 1 uF. Strapping pins 3, 45, 46 left unconnected."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 34.29 170.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d32307b3-bbce-4933-afe9-4ef2dd632228")
	)
